# platform.pizero.sdcard

The RP2350-PiZero's TF socket in its native 4-bit SD mode through
mm.sdcard's SdioCard on mm.mcu's sdio facility: clock GP30, CMD GP31, and
DAT0 to DAT3 on GP40 to GP43, from Waveshare's RP2350-PiZero schematic --
pins only the RP2350B has, which is why the board builds against the SDK's
own PiZero header, and which the Pico implementation reaches through a PIO
block's upper GPIO window. rp2350_pizero binds it and rp2350_pizero_usb_host
inherits it. The card is identified at 400 kHz and runs at 25 MHz, which the
PIO divider rounds down to what clk_sys allows.
